# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  TheOGPirateBot — environment variables
#
#  COPY TO `.env.local` ONLY IF YOU NEED TO OVERRIDE SOMETHING.
#
#  Nothing here is required: every value below has a working default compiled
#  into the code, which is why the repo has never needed a .env to build or run.
#  A GitHub "Download ZIP" therefore loses NOTHING — this file exists so the
#  names are written down in one place.
#
#  There are NO SECRETS in this project's client. Firebase's web config is a
#  public client configuration, not a secret; the TMDB key lives only in the
#  Cloudflare Worker (`worker/.dev.vars`, or `wrangler secret put`).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Same-origin API + proxy (default: https://theogpiratebot.to)
# VITE_ACCOUNT_API_BASE=https://theogpiratebot.to

# Local Node account service during `npm run dev`
# VITE_ACCOUNT_API_DEV_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:3014

# Comma-separated TMDB proxy bases, tried in order BEFORE the built-in ladder
# (src/lib/proxyTiers.js). Point this at your own worker once you deploy one.
# VITE_PROXY_BASES=https://your-worker.workers.dev

# A different Firebase project (public web config — not a secret)
# VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
# VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
#
# THE DOMAIN MOVE SWITCH. The site is theogpiratebot.to as of 2026-11-27, but
# sign-in still deliberately uses Firebase's own host (src/config/authDomain.js)
# because Firebase Hosting only answers /__/auth/handler on a host it is
# connected to. Once the .to apex is connected in Firebase → Hosting AND
# https://theogpiratebot.to/__/auth/handler is an authorised redirect URI on the
# Google OAuth client, set this — no code change, nothing else to do:
# VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=theogpiratebot.to
# VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
# VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
# VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
# VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Android / TV build (not read by Vite)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# versionCode for the in-app updater. CI sets it to the GitHub run number, so
# every published APK knows how old it is. For a local build:
#   OGPB_VERSION_CODE=118 ./gradlew assembleDebug
# OGPB_VERSION_CODE=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Worker (server-side; this is where the only real secret goes)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# cp worker/.dev.vars.example worker/.dev.vars   then put your TMDB key in it.
# In production:  wrangler secret put TMDB_API_KEY
